{{- /*
A quantity carried on the drawn value rather than fixed by a stamp.

Read off the fixture the pool draws from, so the number the law advances
past and the number the writes ask for cannot drift apart: restating it
as a literal would leave two places to change and one of them silent.

The largest member, because the law holds every value it draws to one
number — see perValueQuantity, which says why the smallest would report
a correct store as broken. `max` of one argument is the argument, so a
pool with no second member renders without a special case.
*/ -}}
{{- define "model.lawfield.FixtureQuantity" -}}
{{ .Name }}: max({{ range $i, $read := .Reads }}{{ if $i }}, {{ end }}{{ $read }}{{ end }})
{{- end -}}
